 <nathanael.hannebert@vates.tech>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:52:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs: link to the getting started guide on
 docs.xen-orchestra.com

User guides now live on docs.xen-orchestra.com; keep the README short
and point to it, to avoid duplicated and diverging instructions.
---
 README.md                          | 8 +++++---
 docs/installation-configuration.md | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 37d3b5b..a31e275 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@ The Xen Orchestra Provider lets you manage [Xen Orchestra](https://github.com/va
 
 ![XO logo](./logo_xo.png)
 
+📖 **Getting started**: deploy your first VM in TypeScript, Python, Go, C# or YAML with the [step-by-step guide in the Xen Orchestra documentation](https://docs.xen-orchestra.com/automation/pulumi-provider).
+
 ## Installing
 
 This package is available for several languages/platforms:
@@ -35,7 +37,7 @@ pip install pulumi-xenorchestra
 To use from Go, use `go get` to grab the latest version of the library:
 
 ```bash
-go get github.com/vatesfr/pulumi-xenorchestra/sdk
+go get github.com/vatesfr/pulumi-xenorchestra/sdk/v2
 ```
 
 ### .NET
@@ -54,7 +56,7 @@ The following configuration points are available for the `xenorchestra` provider
 
 - `xenorchestra:url` (environment: `XOA_URL`) - the URL for the Xen Orchestra websockets endpoint. Starts with `wss://`
 Set either:
-- `xenorchestra:username` (environment: `XOA_USERNAME`) - the username for Xen Orchestra
+- `xenorchestra:username` (environment: `XOA_USER`) - the username for Xen Orchestra
 - `xenorchestra:password` (environment: `XOA_PASSWORD`) - the password for Xen Orchestra
 Or:
 - `xenorchestra:token` (environment: `XOA_TOKEN`) - API token for Xen Orchestra
@@ -63,7 +65,7 @@ Or:
 
 ## Usage
 
-See [docs](./docs/_index.md) for examples.
+See the [getting started guide](https://docs.xen-orchestra.com/automation/pulumi-provider) and the [registry examples](./docs/_index.md).
 
 ## Building
 
diff --git a/docs/installation-configuration.md b/docs/installation-configuration.md
index 8740ca9..741ff23 100644
--- a/docs/installation-configuration.md
+++ b/docs/installation-configuration.md
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ The following configuration points are available for the `xenorchestra` provider
 
 - `xenorchestra:url` (environment: `XOA_URL`) - the URL for the Xen Orchestra websockets endpoint. Starts with `wss://`
 Set either:
-- `xenorchestra:username` (environment: `XOA_USERNAME`) - the username for Xen Orchestra
+- `xenorchestra:username` (environment: `XOA_USER`) - the username for Xen Orchestra
 - `xenorchestra:password` (environment: `XOA_PASSWORD`) - the password for Xen Orchestra
 Or:
 - `xenorchestra:token` (environment: `XOA_TOKEN`) - API token for Xen Orchestra
@@ -44,5 +44,5 @@ Or:
 - `xenorchestra:insecure` (environment: `XOA_INSECURE`) - set to any value to disable SSL verification, false by default. Only use if you are using a self-signed certificate and know what you are doing.
 
 
-To get a token you can use the [xo-cli](https://docs.xen-orchestra.com/architecture#xo-cli-cli) or the XO GUI (under User > Authentication tokens).
+To create a token, see [Authenticate your tools](https://docs.xen-orchestra.com/automation/authentication) in the Xen Orchestra documentation. For a step-by-step guide in every language, see the [Pulumi getting started guide](https://docs.xen-orchestra.com/automation/pulumi-provider).
 
